,,//Scene Break//,,

[[=image https://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/theme%3Aclassic/scp_foundation_logo.png class="scene-break"]]

{{@@[[=image URL_HERE class="scene-break"]]@@}}

A {{scene-break}} is an ornamental symbol that “signals a pause for the reader and a transition in the narrative.”

Scene breaks are a classic print convention. Here is an example of one from //[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Section_(typography)#/media/File:Section_break_01_by_Pengo.jpg Alice's Adventures in Wonderland]//. On the SCP Wiki, a {{scene-break}} would be most appropriate in Tale writing.
----
,,//Scene Break + Tinted Icon//,,

[[=image https://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/theme%3Aclassic/scp_foundation_logo.png class="scene-break icon-tint"]]

{{@@[[=image URL_HERE class="scene-break icon-tint"]]@@}}

@@ @@

{{icon-tint}} should only be used in tandem with black logos. Control the icon's color by modifying the {{@@--@@hue}} variable inside {{[[module CSS]]}}:

[[div class="code terminal terminal--dark"]]
##var(--c-builtin)|@@--@@hue##: ##var(--c-value)|#deg##;
[[/div]]

Replace {{#}} with your desired positive integer. Default is {{325deg}}.
----
,,//ListPages Navigator -- First Page//,,
[[div class="listPagesNav"]]
  [[div class="listPagesNav-next"]]
[# Next Iteration ▷]
  [[/div]]
[[/div]]

@@ @@

{{@@[[div class="listPagesNav"]]@@}}
{{@@[[div class="listPagesNav-next"]]@@}}
@@[/offset/1 Next Iteration ▷]@@
{{@@[[/div]]@@}}
{{@@[[/div]]@@}}
----
,,//ListPages Navigator -- Subsequent Pages//,,
[[div class="listPagesNav"]]
  [[div class="listPagesNav-next"]]
[# Next Iteration ▷]
  [[/div]]
  [[div class="listPagesNav-prev"]]
[# ◁ Back]
  [[/div]]
[[/div]]

{{next}} must always go first:

{{@@[[div class="listPagesNav"]]@@}}
{{@@[[div class="listPagesNav-next"]]@@}}
@@[/offset/1 Next Iteration ▷]@@
{{@@[[/div]]@@}}

{{@@[[div class="listPagesNav-prev"]]@@}}
@@[/offset/0 ◁ Back]@@
{{@@[[/div]]@@}}
{{@@[[/div]]@@}}
----
